 ## Background
-The DA-DWT was introduced in the context of wavelet-based volumetric medical image compression, specifically as an enhancement to the JP3D standard [S1]. It addresses the limitations of fixed-direction transforms in medical imaging (CT, MRI) where anatomical structures often have smooth, non-axis-aligned orientations [S1]. The method performs an exhaustive search over a predefined set of direction vectors to achieve transform optimality, differing from previous works that used restricted searches [S1].
